# Curated ADIF parser fixtures -- the sanctioned exception to the root's *.adi
# ignore, in the same spirit as tr4w/test/corpus/.gitignore.
#
# These 11 files are INPUTS to the unit tests (uTestADIF and friends resolve
# them from ParamStr(0), not the working directory), so they are source, not
# operating data. Without this re-include a new fixture would need `git add -f`
# and would otherwise be committed as a test that silently reads nothing.
!*.adi
!*.ADI

# The six D7-written binary contest logs in binarylog/ -- INPUTS to
# uTestLogBinaryFile, uTestLogImport and uTestLogRepository, and the only place
# reading a D7 .TRW is covered since the golden corpus's input became a log.db
# (2026-09-24; NY4I: "that becomes a unit test and not the corpus").  The root
# ignores *.TRW so real operating logs are never committed; these are curated
# fixtures and re-include themselves here, exactly as the corpus set does.
!binarylog/*.trw
!binarylog/*.TRW
